-- title:
--   Level 3B bump vector in a twisted principal-series Whittaker model
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero prime $p$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ and a triple $\lambda=(\lambda_0,\lambda_1,\lambda_2)$ of homomorphisms $(\mathbb Q_p)^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ that are locally constant and unitary ($\|\lambda_i(x)\|=1$ for all $x$). Let $W_2:\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_p)\to\mathbb C$ be nonzero and of the form $W_2=\mathtt{coefficientFn}\,\Lambda\,f$ for some $f$ in the principal series $\mathtt{principalSeries3}\,p\,\lambda$ (locally constant functions invariant under left translation by the upper unipotent matrices $\mathtt{upperUnipotent3}$ and transforming under the diagonal torus by $\lambda$ times the half-modulus) and some linear functional $\Lambda$ on that space which is Whittaker for $\psi_p^{-1}$, i.e. $\Lambda$ applied to the right translate by $\mathtt{upperUnipotent3}\,x\,y\,z$ equals $\psi_p^{-1}(x+y)\Lambda$. Let $\chi$ be a unitary character of $(\mathbb Q_p)^\times$ and $d\ge 1$ an integer such that every $\lambda_i\chi^{-1}$ is trivial on $\mathtt{higherUnitsAt}\,\mathbb Q\,p\,d$, the units $u$ with $|u|=1$ and $|u-1|\le q^{-d}$. Assume further that the cyclic subspace $\mathtt{gl3CyclicSubspace}\,W_2$ (the $\mathbb C$-span of the right translates of $W_2$) contains a nonzero $W'$ whose $\chi\circ\det$-untwist is right invariant under the depth-$d$ congruence subgroup, in the sense that $\chi(\det(gk))^{-1}W'(gk)=\chi(\det g)^{-1}W'(g)$ for all $g$ and all $k$ in $\mathtt{localMaximalCompact3}$ all of whose entries satisfy $|k_{ij}-\delta_{ij}|\le q^{-d}$. Finally let $\xi$ be a unitary character with $\mathtt{HasConductorExponentAt}\,\mathbb Q\,p\,\xi\,B$ (trivial on $\mathtt{higherUnitsAt}$ at level $B$ and nontrivial on each lower level), with $2d+1\le B$. The conclusion asserts the existence of $W_0$ in the cyclic subspace generated by the twisted model $g\mapsto \xi(\det g)\chi(\det g)^{-1}W_2(g)$ such that: $W_0$ is right invariant under $\mathtt{congruenceK1}\,(\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q})\,\mathbb Q\,p\,(3B)$, the set of $k\in\mathtt{localMaximalCompact3}$ with $|k_{20}|,|k_{21}|,|k_{22}-1|\le q^{-3B}$; the restriction of $W_0$ along the embedding $\mathtt{iotaGL}:\mathrm{GL}_2\to\mathrm{GL}_3$ is right invariant under $\mathtt{AdelicDock.localLevelOne}\,(\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q})\,\mathbb Q\,p\,\top$; that restriction vanishes off the set of $h$ of the form $\mathtt{unipotentGL2}\,x\cdot k$ with $x\in\mathbb Q_p$ and $k$ in that same subgroup; and $W_0(\mathtt{iotaGL}\,1)=1$.
--
--   This produces, at the place $p$, the normalised "bump" vector supported on $N_2\,\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Z_p)$ inside a deeply twisted principal-series Whittaker model on $\mathrm{GL}_3$, the local datum against which the $\mathrm{GL}_3\times\mathrm{GL}_2$ Rankin–Selberg integral at $p$ is computed. It is the input to the local-integral evaluation step [`LanglandsTunnell.RankinSelberg.forall_mem_span_rsLocalIntegral_dual_eq_mul_of_forall_localZeta31_fe_of_deepTwist_of_principalLevel_of_admissible_of_gammaFactor_of_forall_localZeta31_fe_of_bump_levelShift_global`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.RankinSelberg.forall_mem_span_rsLocalIntegral_dual_eq_mul_of_forall_localZeta31_fe_of_deepTwist_of_principalLevel_of_admissible_of_gammaFactor_of_forall_localZeta31_fe_of_bump_levelShift_global) in the converse-theorem route to Langlands–Tunnell.
